    "text": "Radio waves coming at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∠</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></math> to vertical are received by radar after reflection from a nearby water surface and directly. The height of the antenna from the water surface so that it records a maximum intensity, should be (wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></math>)<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-06-15_at_3.32.30_PM.jpeg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 186px;\" />",
